{
  "design_rationale": "First-order self-draining heater with positive gain needs steady power. Measured equilibria u=0->0.206, 0.25->0.491, 0.27->0.501, 0.30->0.53 give overall K~1.1 and local K~0.5-0.8, tau~150s, delay<30s, no deadzone near target, one-sided negative spikes. Hence feedforward 0.26 for y=0.5 plus PI on outlier-rejected low-passed measurement. Kp=1.0 gives closed-loop ~65s tau without delay instability, Ki=0.012 trims offset, gated to |e|<0.15 plus saturation freeze to prevent windup during 0.2->0.5 heat-up. Clip +-0.045 plus 15s filter rejects 0.05-0.13 spikes while tracking 0.006/s true rate. Integral +-0.15/0.20 leaves >0.13 authority to fix feedforward error, u capped 0.75 for 0.10 margin to soft 0.85/hard 0.90.",
  "machine_card": "Heater: up means hotter. Gain positive: overall (0.53-0.206)/0.3~1.08, local near 0.5 ~0.5-0.8 (0.05 step gave 0.039, 0.02 step gave 0.01). Speed: lag <30s, first-order tau 120-200s (~150s), settling ~400s; worst rate 0.006/s. Deadzone <0.02 near target. Self-draining: u=0 settles to 0.18-0.25 (~0.206), does not hold. Holding for y=0.5 is u~0.26 in [0.25,0.27]: 0.25 holds 0.491, 0.27 holds 0.501, 0.30 holds 0.53. Noise: baseline jitter +-0.01-0.02 plus frequent brief negative-only spikes 0.05-0.13 to 0.40-0.47; use median/mode not minima.",
  "operator_note": "Hands-off regulator for 0.5 +-0.025. Heats at ~0.55 then eases to ~0.26. Ignores brief temperature dips. Keeps power below 0.75 to stay clear of 0.85/0.90 limits. Do not add manual bias; integral trims offset in a few minutes.",
  "predicted_behavior": "From cold ~0.2, u~0.56 rising with tau~65s, reaches 0.35 in ~80s then integral enables, enters 0.475-0.525 in ~150-220s with no overshoot past 0.60 true. After 300s stays in band, jitter +-0.015 true, spikes invisible in true state. Steady u~0.24-0.28 (feedforward 0.26 plus +-0.05 trim), overshoot <0.02, MAE after settling <0.015, energy near minimum holding power.",
